<title>FRANCE: French June consumer sentiment improves.</title>
<headline>French June consumer sentiment improves.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE gave the following data on Wednesday on household opinions. A positive figure shows the percentage points by which the percentage of respondents saying things had improved or risen outnumbered the percentage saying things had worsened.</p>
<p>				    June   May   Apr  Mar  Feb Jan  Dec</p>
<p> Overall			  -23   -33   -32  -32  -30  -30  -32</p>
<p> Past living standards	-61   -66   -62  -64  -63  -67  -66</p>
<p> Future living standards    -10   -39   -41  -39  -36  -35  -38</p>
<p> Future unemployment	   36    63    64   63   51   60   55</p>
<p> Past inflation		 -55   -53   -53  -51  -50  -44  -52</p>
<p> Future inflation	     -55   -42   -43  -41  -39  -35  -37</p>
<p> Good time to spend	   -27   -31   -26  -26  -24  -23  -25</p>
<p> Good time to save	     52    51    48   52   52   52   50</p>
<p> Current personal finances    8     8     9    9   10   10    9</p>
<p> Past personal finances     -19   -22   -21  -21  -20  -20  -21</p>
<p> Future personal finances     2    -7    -7   -8   -6   -6   -8</p>
<p> Ability to save		-29   -32   -31  -26  -27  -29  -29</p>
<p>NOTE - INSEE said consumer sentiment had also improved sharply after the parliamentary election in March 1993 and presidential election in May 1995. The survey was the first since a Socialist-led government was brought to power in a parliamentary election on June 1.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
